  "market_context": "Uptrend on GER40 daily chart with higher highs and higher lows; price pulled back after an impulse move, forming a retracement zone where RSI showed lower low while price made higher low.",
  "key_observation": "Price formed a higher low while RSI formed a lower low—classic hidden bullish divergence—and the Fibonacci retracement of the prior impulse move landed precisely at the 0.618 level, creating confluence for a long entry.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified market structure with higher highs and higher lows, focusing specifically on the sequence of two consecutive higher lows in price.",
    "Step 2: Compared RSI values at those two price lows and observed that RSI made a lower low despite price making a higher low, confirming a hidden bullish divergence.",
    "Step 3: Drew Fibonacci retracement from the swing low to the subsequent swing high of the impulse move, noting the pullback terminated exactly at the 0.618 level.",
    "Step 4: Recognized confluence between the hidden divergence and the 0.618 Fibonacci retracement (Gold Zone), labeling it a 'golden entry signal'."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Hidden divergences on higher time frames gain high probability when aligned with Fibonacci retracement zones—especially the 0.618 level. Never trade retracements alone; require momentum confirmation via RSI divergence.",
